<!--Post: 9242--><!--Time: 1109443486-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9242"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Angrywolf<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Angrywolf<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 26, 2005 - 10:44 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->ooooo..a lot of viciousness here..as BTK has been caught..and none of us were ever his &#34;fans&#34;...he was a vicious killer...imagine if he had been in your city..killing your relatives..so I feel a duty to defend the people who have come here and speculated about BTK and say I believe we all wanted him caught and there are no regrets he has been caught...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9242-->
<!--Post: 9243--><!--Time: 1109443643-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9243"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 26, 2005 - 10:47 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->One of those British guys was a cop. I don&#39;t recall the name I guess. I do remember a photo of a policeman&#39;s book, and the inscription read something like &#34;If you intend to steal this, read page [whatever it was].&#34; The page mentioned concerned the punishment for theft. This was also the guy who buried bodies underneath the floor of his flat. I wish I could remember the name.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
